# Google Play destination

Ward is intended for **publication on Google Play (Android)**. Treat that as a product constraint in every relevant change:

1. Prefer Capacitor/Android paths that stay Play-compliant (permissions, privacy, target SDK, 64-bit, app bundles when releasing).
2. Store listing assets belong under Drive `store/icons/` and `store/listing/`; keep icons and screenshots Play-policy safe.
3. When building for distribution, prefer **release** artifacts (`bundleRelease` / signed AAB when available) over debug APKs for upload; still copy outputs to `G:\My Drive\Ward\releases\apk\` (or `releases/archive/` for older builds).
4. Avoid features that block Play review without an explicit user decision (background location, deceptive ads, IP/scraped assets, closed third-party content).
5. Keep `applicationId` / package naming and versionCode/versionName coherent with Play Console uploads.
6. Call out Play implications briefly when a change affects permissions, networking, billing, content rating, or store assets.
